{
  "_doc": "#796 THE change sets the fleet is measured by: for each, cloud_android_ci_fanout.py --scenarios prints how many workflow runs GitHub starts and -- the number that costs 30 minutes and a phone update each -- how many app APKs, lib APKs and rootfs companions the publish gates would actually rebuild. `expect` is what 1_cicd/src/scripts/test/rebuild-fanout.test.sh (mesh-membership-guard, every push) holds the tree to, both ways: more rebuilt than expected is a fan-out regression (a lib newly compiled into apps, a trigger list widened, a slice that stopped being per-root); fewer is progress that must be locked in by lowering the number in the same commit, so it cannot creep back. `ship` is a ceiling only (a guard added or removed changes `runs`, which is reported, not held). Files are paths as a push would list them; they need not exist (a new file in a watched directory fires the same triggers as an edited one). Every entry names a real cause from the 30 days to 2026-10-03: #783 (core), #792 (devtools, the port table), #791 (sysdns, one engine), #790 (one app), #771 (rootfs declaration), and the 17 verify-rootfs.sh edits that each republished 437 MB. #836: `refresh` is how many apps fleet-refresh.yml ships LATER for the change (their deferred shared-lib inputs moved; they are NOT started per push), held both ways like the rest. A static shared lib edit starts EVERY app that compiles it (an edit under libs:bottomnav alone once left Cloud Store unshipped) plus the one lib-APK builder run. #870 (owner rule, see rebuild-isolation.json): only RUNTIME ENGINES ship a Cloud-Lib APK (discovered by the ENGINE CONTRACT manifest scan, cloud-android-lib-apks-engines.py), so an engine lib change = 1 lib APK, 0 apps; a static lib change = every app that compiles it, 0 libs (`refresh` is only for deferred cross-app dirs, so it is 0 here); a shared manifest change = 0 apps. cloud-android-rebuild-isolation-guard.py asserts this independently of the counts.",
